    <div class="verdict">
      <strong>The honest verdict:</strong> if you bill over $2,500/month and accept card payments through your invoicing tool, Wave costs you more than FreshBooks Premium in pure fees. The "free" pricing stops being free somewhere around $1,500/month of paid invoices.
    </div>

    <h2>When Wave is the right choice</h2>
    <p>Honestly: Wave is great for some people. If you want full double-entry accounting, payroll, inventory, and invoicing all in one tool — and your clients don't pay by card through the platform — Wave is the best free option out there. The accounting suite is genuinely good. We don't compete with that.</p>

    <p>What Wave is not great for: solo freelancers billing primarily via card payments. The 2.9% cut eats your margin.</p>

    <h2>When FreshBooks is the right choice</h2>
    <p>FreshBooks is the right choice if you need:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Time tracking built in</li>
      <li>Team collaboration (multiple users on one account)</li>
      <li>Project management features</li>
      <li>Recurring billing / subscriptions</li>
      <li>A full accounting suite that includes invoicing</li>
    </ul>

    <p>What FreshBooks is not great for: solo freelancers who don't need any of the above. The $17/mo starting tier caps you at 5 clients — fine for someone with 3 clients, brutal if you have 6.</p>

    <h2>What about InvoiceFast.ca?</h2>
    <p>InvoiceFast.ca is a popular Canadian-only invoicing app with a strong mobile presence (native iOS + Android apps), $3.99/month or $79.99 lifetime pricing, and 1,000+ contractor users in Canada.</p>

    <h3>Where InvoiceFast is genuinely good</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Mobile-first:</strong> actual native iOS and Android apps, designed for contractors who invoice from job sites</li>
      <li><strong>Cheapest subscription:</strong> $3.99/month is half what JustInvoice costs after launch</li>
      <li><strong>Lifetime deal:</strong> $79.99 one-time — great for "I'll never subscribe to anything" buyers</li>
      <li><strong>Canadian-built:</strong> GST/HST support, contractor-focused templates</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Where InvoiceFast falls short for most freelancers</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No Stripe payments.</strong> Invoices go out as PDFs. Clients must pay by e-Transfer, bank transfer, or cheque. If your client is busy or non-techy, they will not pay the same day. Expect 7-21 days to get paid, often longer.</li>
      <li><strong>Premium template upsells.</strong> The free tier ships with limited templates. Pro templates cost $9 each. Nickel-and-dime pricing.</li>
      <li><strong>$3.99 vs $9 isn't really cheaper</strong> once you factor in: 1) slower payment collection (the real cost), 2) lost Stripe convenience, 3) watermark on free tier.</li>
      <li><strong>Web app feels dated</strong> compared to JustInvoice's modern dark UI.</li>
    </ul>

