        <tr><td>Mobile apps</td><td>Mobile-responsive web (native app on roadmap)</td><td>✓ Native iOS + Android</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lifetime deal</td><td>None</td><td>✓ $79.99 one-time</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Avg days to get paid</td><td>Same day (one click)</td><td>14-30 days (e-Transfer friction)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Premium templates</td><td>All included</td><td>$9 per template pack</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Freelancers who bill via card, want fast payment</td><td>Contractors who invoice from job sites, e-Transfer payers</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="verdict">
      <strong>The honest verdict:</strong> InvoiceFast is a legit competitor with a real customer base. If mobile-first or lifetime pricing matters more to you than payment speed, InvoiceFast is a fine choice. If you've ever lost a week chasing an e-Transfer from a busy client, JustInvoice's one-click Stripe payment will pay for itself on your very first invoice.
    </div>

    <h2>When JustInvoice is the right choice</h2>
    <p>JustInvoice is built for one specific user:</p>

    <blockquote style="border-left: 4px solid var(--blue); padding-left: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; color: var(--ink);">
      Solo freelancer or 1-3 person agency, 5-30 active clients, billing primarily via card or ACH, doesn't need time tracking / inventory / full accounting, in any of 40+ Stripe-supported countries (Canada, US, UK, Australia, EU, etc.), wants to send clean PDF invoices and get paid without fees eating their margin. Configurable tax and currency per account.
    </blockquote>

    <p>That's it. We don't try to be everything for everyone. We try to be the right tool for that specific person.</p>

    <h2>Feature-by-feature honest comparison</h2>

    <h3>Tax handling (GST/HST/PST, US sales tax, UK VAT, custom rates)</h3>
    <p><strong>Winner: JustInvoice for flexibility.</strong> Tax percentage is configurable per account in settings — set GST/HST, US state sales tax, UK VAT, or any custom rate you need. Every invoice automatically applies the right rate. Wave and FreshBooks support common tax scenarios but the configuration is locked behind tier upgrades or awkward workarounds. JustInvoice treats tax as a first-class setting, not a paid add-on.</p>

    <h3>PDF quality</h3>
    <p><strong>Three-way tie.</strong> All three generate clean PDF invoices. Wave and FreshBooks have more template options. JustInvoice keeps it simple — one clean template that looks professional. Pick based on what you actually use.</p>

    <h3>Mobile experience</h3>
    <p><strong>Winner: Wave.</strong> Wave has the best mobile app of the three. FreshBooks mobile is solid. JustInvoice is currently mobile-responsive web only — a native app is on the roadmap.</p>

    <h3>Integrations</h3>
    <p><strong>Winner: FreshBooks.</strong> FreshBooks integrates with 100+ tools. Wave integrates with most of the same. JustInvoice is intentionally minimal — Stripe for payments, Resend for email, that's it.</p>

    <h3>Pricing transparency</h3>
    <p><strong>Winner: JustInvoice.</strong> $9/mo USD flat. No tiers, no caps, no "contact us for pricing." Wave's pricing page requires you to calculate your transaction fees yourself. FreshBooks has 4 tiers and 7 add-ons — easy to accidentally end up at $60/mo when you thought you were paying $17.</p>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Wave really free?</h3>
    <p>The software is free. The payment processing is 2.9% + 60¢ per transaction. For a freelancer billing $50K/year through Wave, that's roughly $1,450 in fees. Not "free" in practice — Wave makes money from your payment processing.</p>

    <h3>Can I import my Wave or FreshBooks invoices into JustInvoice?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Both Wave and FreshBooks let you export invoices and clients as CSV. JustInvoice supports CSV import for both. Migration takes about 20 minutes for a typical freelancer.</p>

    <h3>Does JustInvoice handle recurring billing?</h3>
    <p>Not yet. Recurring invoices are on the roadmap. If recurring billing is a core need, FreshBooks is the better choice today.</p>

    <h3>Can I switch later?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Export your data as CSV from JustInvoice whenever you want. We don't lock your data in.</p>

    <h3>Where does JustInvoice work?</h3>
    <p>Anywhere Stripe works — 40+ countries including Canada, US, UK, Australia, most of EU. Currency is configurable per account (USD, CAD, GBP, EUR, AUD, and more). Tax rate is also configurable — set GST/HST for Canadian clients, US state sales tax, UK VAT, or any custom rate. Each invoice uses your account's configured currency and tax rate.</p>

    <h3>How is JustInvoice different from InvoiceFast.ca?</h3>
    <p>InvoiceFast is great for mobile-first contractors who invoice from job sites and clients pay by e-Transfer. JustInvoice is built for freelancers whose clients want to pay by card with one click. If you've ever lost a week waiting for an e-Transfer, that's the difference. If you do most of your invoicing on your phone from a job site and your clients pay by e-Transfer anyway, InvoiceFast is the better choice.</p>

    <h2>Try JustInvoice free during early access</h2>

    <p>Free during early access. After launch, JustInvoice is $9/mo USD flat — no transaction fees, no caps, no surprises. <strong>Watch the 60-second demo above</strong> to see the full invoice flow before you sign up.</p>

